cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Blast Radius and Recovery for Compromised AI Model Lineage
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it. A preprint of the
  accompanying paper is in preparation.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Apoorve
    family-names: Bhargava
    email: apoorve1577@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/apoorve1577/model-lineage-recovery"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-07"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation for "Beyond Detection: A Recovery-Oriented
  Architecture for Compromised AI Model Remediation". Implements a typed
  lineage DAG over model artifacts, a blast-radius query with a proven
  soundness property, and a recovery planner that classifies each affected
  artifact by whether rollback to a clean signed ancestor is available.
  Evaluated by running queries against an incompletely recorded graph and
  scoring them against ground truth they never see.
keywords:
  - AI supply chain security
  - model provenance
  - blast radius
  - incident response
  - software supply chain
